# ML Core layer for Linux
# Platform-specific lockfile for deterministic pip-compile resolution.
#
# This file is Linux-specific because pip-compile cannot resolve
# conditional dependencies across platforms in a single graph.
#
# Run `make compile` in this directory to generate pinned ml-core-linux.txt
#
# PLATFORM TARGET: linux-* (Linux Intel/AMD/ARM)
#   - linux-x86_64-cpu    (Linux Intel/AMD, CPU baseline)
#   - linux-x86_64-cuda   (Linux Intel/AMD, NVIDIA GPU)
#   - linux-arm64-cpu     (Linux ARM, CPU-only)
#
# SECURITY NOTE (CVE-2025-32434):
#   torch < 2.6.0 has a critical RCE vulnerability (CVSS 9.8) via torch.load()
#   All Linux platforms use torch 2.6.0+ (secure)
#
# See: requirements/README.md for layering rationale.

# --- PyTorch (Linux, security-aware) ---
# SECURITY: torch 2.6.0+ required to patch CVE-2025-32434 (torch.load RCE)
torch>=2.6.0,<3  # CVE-2025-32434 patched
torchvision>=0.21.0,<1  # matches torch 2.6.0+

